 "intro": "Rejecting one reason and giving the real one, and other finer ways of stating a cause.",
 "palabras": [
  {
   "palabra": "no es que",
   "significado": "it's not that",
   "pron": "no es ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It always takes the subjunctive: «no es que esté enfadada». «Es que» with the real reason usually follows.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "sino que",
   "significado": "but rather (before a verb)",
   "pron": "SI-no ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is written as one word and follows a negative: «no lloro, sino que río». It is not «si no».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "no porque",
   "significado": "not because",
   "pron": "no POR-ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It rejects a cause with the subjunctive: «no porque quiera». The true one goes with «sino porque».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "dado que",
   "significado": "given that",
   "pron": "DA-do ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It presents a known cause and takes the indicative: «dado que no vienes». It is formal.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "en vista de que",
   "significado": "seeing that",
   "pron": "en BIS-ta de ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It presents an already known reason, with the indicative: «en vista de que llueve».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "a fuerza de",
   "significado": "by dint of",
   "pron": "a FWER-tha de",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It goes with an infinitive: «a fuerza de practicar». The z in «fuerza» sounds «th».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "de tanto",
   "significado": "from so much",
   "pron": "de TAN-to",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It goes with an infinitive: «de tanto leer me duele la cabeza». It expresses cause by excess.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "lo que pasa es que",
   "significado": "the thing is that",
   "pron": "lo ke PA-sa es ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It helps you justify yourself: «lo que pasa es que no tengo tiempo». «Que» and a verb follow.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "por si fuera poco",
   "significado": "as if that weren't enough",
   "pron": "por si FWE-ra PO-ko",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It adds one more problem: «por si fuera poco, llovía». It has «fuera», subjunctive, as a hypothesis.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "agotada",
